Z||000000||Neverfinished||11-01-2001||03:40 PM||||Hey guys.<BR>I'm not sure if this is common with 4 cylinder fiero's (84 SE with poly dogbone)<BR>But when my car is ran at around 2800 RPM it makes the most irritating resonance inside the cockpit. My muffler shop said it wasnt the muffler or the exhaust...<BR>anyone have the same problem? Or can anyone tell me how to get rid of this bwwwwwwwwwaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa noise.<BR>thanks everyone<BR>||||reg||13
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||11-01-2001||06:02 PM||||hehe, I have the Fiero Stores Ultimate Poly Dogbone in my 84SE 4 speed and it does the same thing. Its only at lower 2000 RPM in any gear or even when the cars not moving.<P>When I had the poly dogbone in my automatic 88 coupe , it was really bad at anything under 1500rpm, or while the trans was in drive. So bad infact I took it out and put the stock rubber one back in when I sold the car. I dont think anyone would have bought it because it shaked so badly!<P>Only reason I keep the on in my 84SE is because the other mounts are shot. I need something to hold the engine in place. Its also kind of sporty and dosen't bug me because I just commute 20 miles a day in the car.||||reg||10
Z||000002||baptistheart||11-01-2001||06:10 PM||||I have that dogbone too, and it does the same thing, first three mounths after i got it my positive cable worked loose from the bat., then my neg. cable, then my thermostat houseing started leaking. Yep the bolts were loose.<P> Needless to say i think it's too stiff and am going to change back to the o.e.m.<P>------------------<BR>Joe||||reg||1
