Z||000007||Neverfinished||11-01-2001||07:59 PM||||Voytek-<BR>I had the cash in my hand to go buy that daytona and backed out as i had all the papers done just waiting for my sig...<BR>I couldn't get rid of my fiero after putting sooo much time into it. I also put 17's on it with bf goodrich scorcher T/A 's.<P>By the way...<BR>I went to my local gm dealer and talked with him about the resonance.<BR>alot of new cars have this same problem too.<BR>apparently if you move around a special weight clamped to the exhaust system it will kill the vibration and that noise. My dad has one kicking around here off his LT1 police cruiser and I will slap that on tomorrow after work.<BR>I will keep you guys up to date if it fixes the problem...<P>Voytek, Nice to see you still remember me.<BR>Next time you are in town give me a call.<BR>or e-mail me.<BR>smokindakron@hotmail.com||||reg||10
Z||000008||theogre||11-01-2001||08:09 PM||||If anyone has a 4 cyl poly dogbone you are chucking, I need one for some testing.<P>My thought is the polly is too stiff but the OE rubber just won't work on my 87. (Read the cave article about dog bones if you haven't already.)<P>I want to alter the bushings to see how I can make it a little softer but I don't want to risk trashing the only good strut I have.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
